384 :         }
385 :         pos.setIndex(endIndex);
```

The issue is that this code assumes the length of the imaginary character to be a specific number of characters and directly compares it with the substring of the source string at that location. If the length of the imaginary character is not correctly set or if the source string is shorter than expected, it can lead to a `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`.

The failing test `testForgottenImaginaryCharacter` tries to parse a complex number without specifying the imaginary part, leading to this exception.

