Title: Diagnosis
Details: The current bug report describes a `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` in the `parse` method of the `ComplexFormat` class. The issue occurs when parsing the imaginary character without checking whether it is set or not. The code directly compares a substring of the source string with the imaginary character, leading to the exception if the lengths mismatch or the imaginary character is not present. The failing test `testForgottenImaginaryCharacter` invokes the `parse` method without specifying the imaginary part, triggering the exception.
Further investigation is needed to confirm the exact conditions triggering the exception and to implement proper handling to avoid `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException`.

